From a6d45ac207d399f423e3af57120dc02d750c516c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knaox <djamvn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: add wlhostvk context rendering into a host wl_surface

--gpu-context=wlhostvk takes a struct mpv_wlhost_target (wl_display and
wl_surface of the embedding application) from --wid and renders into the
surface with no Wayland connection, window or input of its own;
--wlhostvk-surface-size sets the swapchain size (VOCTRL_EXTERNAL_RESIZE).
HDR goes through the Vulkan WSI color spaces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
