@@ -7144,6 +7144,13 @@ them.
 
     macOS with ``--gpu-context=moltenvk`` only.
 
+``--wlhostvk-surface-size=<WxH>``
+    Size, in pixels, of the swapchain for ``--gpu-context=wlhostvk``. There is
+    no window: the embedding application owns the ``wl_surface`` passed with
+    ``--wid`` (its role, position, scale and viewport) and must set its size.
+
+    Wayland with ``--gpu-context=wlhostvk`` only.
+
 ``--gpu-sw``
     Continue even if a software renderer is detected. This only works with
     OpenGL/Vulkan backends. For d3d11, see ``--d3d11-warp``.
@@ -7198,6 +7205,12 @@ them.
         Vulkan on macOS (MoltenVK) into a ``CAMetalLayer`` owned by the
         embedding application. Requires ``--wid`` be set to that layer; see
         ``--moltenvk-surface-size``.
+    wlhostvk
+        Vulkan on Wayland into a ``wl_surface`` owned by the embedding
+        application (usually a subsurface below its own surface). Requires
+        ``--wid`` be set to a pointer to ``struct mpv_wlhost_target``
+        (``video/out/vulkan/context_wlhost.c``); see
+        ``--wlhostvk-surface-size``. Never auto-probed.
 
     This is an object settings list option. See `List Options`_ for details.
 
